pan><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0715em;\">K</span></span></span></span> is the <strong>loop gain</strong>. When <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">∣</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">L</span><span class=\"mord\">∣</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">≫</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6444em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">1</span></span></span></span>, <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.1389em;\">T</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">≈</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6444em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">1</span></span></span></span> whatever <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">G</span></span></span></span> is.</p>\n<p>How much does <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.1389em;\">T</span></span></span></span> move when <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">G</span></span></span></span> moves? Differentiate:</p>\n<div class=\"math-scroll\"><span class=\"katex-display\"><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:2.363em;vertical-align:-0.936em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mopen nulldelimiter\"></span><span class=\"mfrac\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:1.427em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.314em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">d</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">G</span><span class=\"mord\">/</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">G</span></span></span><span style=\"top:-3.23em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"frac-line\" style=\"border-bottom-width:0.04em;\"></span></span><span style=\"top:-3.677em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">d</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.1389em;\">T</span><span class=\"mord\">/</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.1389em;\">T</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.936em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mclose nulldelimiter\"></span></span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:2.0908em;vertical-align:-0.7693em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mopen nulldelimiter\"></span><span class=\"mfrac\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:1.3214em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.314em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord\">1</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">+</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">G</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0715em;\">K</span></span></span><span style=\"top:-3.23em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"frac-line\" style=\"border-bottom-width:0.04em;\"></span></span><span style=\"top:-3.677em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord\">1</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.7693em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mclose nulldelimiter\"></span></span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0576em;\">S</span><span class=\"mord\">.</span></span></span></span></span></div>\n<p><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0576em;\">S</span></span></span></span> is the <strong>sensitivity function</strong>. With a loop gain of 20, a 30 % plant change moves the output by about <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">30/21</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">≈</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6444em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">1.4</span></span></span></span> %.</p>\n<p>The price: the sensor must be accurate, because the loop makes <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.625em;vertical-align:-0.1944em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0359em;\">y</span></span></span></span> follow the measured value, errors included. And high gain risks instability, the subject of the rest of this phase.</p>\n\n<figure class=\"fig\"><div class=\"fig-body\"><div class=\"widget\" data-widget=\"fbrobust\" data-args=\"{}\"></div></div><figcaption>The same plant with open-loop and closed-loop control. Move the true plant gain away from the model and watch the open-loop output follow the error while the closed-loop output barely moves.</figcaption></figure>\n<h2 id=\"worked-example\">Worked example</h2>\n<p>Plant <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">G</span><span class=\"mopen\">(</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">s</span><span class=\"mclose\">)</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">2/</span><span class=\"mopen\">(</span><span class=\"mord\">0.5</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">s</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">+</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">1</span><span class=\"mclose\">)</span></span></span></span> modelled exactly; proportional controller <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0715em;\">K</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6444em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">10</span></span></span></span>, so <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">L</span><span class=\"mopen\">(</span><span class=\"mord\">0</span><span class=\"mclose\">)</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6444em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">20</span></span></span></span>. A prefilter <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">1/</span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.1389em;\">T</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.3011em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.55em;margin-left:-0.1389em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">0</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.15em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mopen\">(</span><span class=\"mord\">0</span><span class=\"mclose\">)</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">21/20</span></span></span></span> makes the nominal closed loop reach exactly <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.4306em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0278em;\">r</span></span></span></span>.</p>\n<ol>\n<li>True gain +30 % (<span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">G</span><span class=\"mopen\">(</span><span class=\"mord\">0</span><span class=\"mclose\">)</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6444em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">2.6</span></span></span></span>): <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">L</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6444em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">26</span></span></span></span>, <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.1389em;\">T</span><span class=\"mopen\">(</span><span class=\"mord\">0</span><span class=\"mclose\">)</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">26/27</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6444em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">0.9630</span></span></span></span>. With the prefilter, output <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.3669em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.7278em;vertical-align:-0.0833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">0.9630</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">×</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">21/20</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6444em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">1.0111</span></span></span></span>: an 1.1 % error, against 30 % open loop. 27 times smaller.</li>\n<li>True gain −30 %: <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">L</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6444em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">14</span></span></span></span>, <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.1389em;\">T</span><span class=\"mopen\">(</span><span class=\"mord\">0</span><span class=\"mclose\">)</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6444em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">0.9333</span></span></span></span>, output 0.980: a 2.0 % error, 15 times smaller.</li>\n<li>Bonus: the closed-loop time constant is <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">0.5/</span><span class=\"mopen\">(</span><span class=\"mord\">1</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">+</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">20</span><span class=\"mclose\">)</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6444em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">24</span></span></span></span> ms instead of 0.5 s.</li>\n</ol>\n<h2 id=\"code-it-from-scratch\">Code it from scratch</h2>\n\n<div class=\"code-card\" data-code=\"0\"><div class=\"code-head\"><span class=\"fname\" translate=\"no\">feedback.py</span><button class=\"btn btn-quiet btn-small\" type=\"button\" data-copy=\"0\">Copy</button><button class=\"btn btn-quiet btn-small\" type=\"button\" data-download=\"0\">Download</button></div><pre tabindex=\"0\"><code class=\"language-python\"><span class=\"hljs-keyword\">import</span> numpy <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">as</span> np\n\ntau, G0 = <span class=\"hljs-number\">0.5</span>, <span class=\"hljs-number\">2.0</span>\nK = <span class=\"hljs-number\">10.0</span>\nL0 = K * G0\npre = (<span class=\"hljs-number\">1</span> + L0) / L0                       <span class=\"hljs-comment\"># prefilter: nominal closed loop has unit DC gain</span>\n\n<span class=\"hljs-keyword\">def</span> <span class=\"hljs-title function_\">simulate</span>(<span class=\"hljs-params\">Gtrue, closed, T=<span class=\"hljs-number\">3.0</span>, dt=<span class=\"hljs-number\">1e-4</span>, r=<span class=\"hljs-number\">1.0</span></span>):\n    y, out = <span class=\"hljs-number\">0.0</span>, []\n    <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">for</span> _ <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">in</span> <span class=\"hljs-built_in\">range</span>(<span class=\"hljs-built_in\">int</span>(T / dt)):\n        u = K * (pre * r - y) <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">if</span> closed <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">else</span> r / G0\n        y += dt * (Gtrue * u - y) / tau    <span class=\"hljs-comment\"># first-order plant, exact enough at this step</span>\n        out.append(y)\n    <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">return</span> np.array(out)\n\n<span class=\"hljs-keyword\">def</span> <span class=\"hljs-title function_\">test_closed_loop_error_ten_times_smaller</span>():\n    <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">for</span> change <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">in</span> (+<span class=\"hljs-number\">0.3</span>, -<span class=\"hljs-number\">0.3</span>):\n        Gt = G0 * (<span class=\"hljs-number\">1</span> + change)\n        e_open = <span class=\"hljs-built_in\">abs</span>(simulate(Gt, <span class=\"hljs-literal\">False</span>)[-<span class=\"hljs-number\">1</span>] - <span class=\"hljs-number\">1</span>)\n        e_closed = <span class=\"hljs-built_in\">abs</span>(simulate(Gt, <span class=\"hljs-literal\">True</span>)[-<span class=\"hljs-number\">1</span>] - <span class=\"hljs-number\">1</span>)\n        Lt = K * Gt\n        predicted = <span class=\"hljs-built_in\">abs</span>(Lt / (<span class=\"hljs-number\">1</span> + Lt) * pre - <span class=\"hljs-number\">1</span>)\n        <span class=\"hljs-built_in\">print</span>(<span class=\"hljs-string\">f&quot;plant gain <span class=\"hljs-subst\">{change:+<span class=\"hljs-number\">.0</span>%}</span>: open-loop error <span class=\"hljs-subst\">{e_open:<span class=\"hljs-number\">.1</span>%}</span>, closed-loop <span class=\"hljs-subst\">{e_closed:<span class=\"hljs-number\">.2</span>%}</span> (predicted <span class=\"hljs-subst\">{predicted:<span class=\"hljs-number\">.2</span>%}</span>), <span class=\"hljs-subst\">{e_open / e_closed:<span class=\"hljs-number\">.0</span>f}</span>x smaller&quot;</span>)\n        <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">assert</span> <span class=\"hljs-built_in\">abs</span>(e_closed - predicted) &lt; <span class=\"hljs-number\">1e-4</span>\n        <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">assert</span> e_open / e_closed &gt; <span class=\"hljs-number\">10</span>\n\n<span class=\"hljs-keyword\">def</span> <span class=\"hljs-title function_\">test_sensitivity_formula</span>():\n    <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">for</span> L <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">in</span> (<span class=\"hljs-number\">1.0</span>, <span class=\"hljs-number\">5.0</span>, <span class=\"hljs-number\">20.0</span>, <span class=\"hljs-number\">100.0</span>):\n        T = <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">lambda</span> g: g * L / (<span class=\"hljs-number\">1</span> + g * L)\n        d = <span class=\"hljs-number\">1e-6</span>\n        rel = (T(<span class=\"hljs-number\">1</span> + d) - T(<span class=\"hljs-number\">1</span> - d)) / (<span class=\"hljs-number\">2</span> * d) / T(<span class=\"hljs-number\">1</span>)\n        <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">assert</span> <span class=\"hljs-built_in\">abs</span>(rel - <span class=\"hljs-number\">1</span> / (<span class=\"hljs-number\">1</span> + L)) &lt; <span class=\"hljs-number\">1e-8</span>\n\n<span class=\"hljs-keyword\">def</span> <span class=\"hljs-title function_\">test_faster</span>():\n    y = simulate(G0, <span class=\"hljs-literal\">True</span>, T=<span class=\"hljs-number\">0.5</span>)\n    t63 = np.argmax(y &gt; <span class=\"hljs-number\">0.632</span> * y[-<span class=\"hljs-number\">1</span>]) * <span class=\"hljs-number\">1e-4</span>\n    <span class=\"hljs-built_in\">print</span>(<span class=\"hljs-string\">f&quot;closed-loop time constant <span class=\"hljs-subst\">{t63 * <span class=\"hljs-number\">1000</span>:<span class=\"hljs-number\">.1</span>f}</span> ms (predicted <span class=\"hljs-subst\">{tau / (<span class=\"hljs-number\">1</span> + L0) * <span class=\"hljs-number\">1000</span>:<span class=\"hljs-number\">.1</span>f}</span> ms)&quot;</span>)\n    <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">assert</span> <span class=\"hljs-built_in\">abs</span>(t63 - tau / (<span class=\"hljs-number\">1</span> + L0)) &lt; <span class=\"hljs-number\">5e-4</span>\n\ntest_closed_loop_error_ten_times_smaller()\ntest_sensitivity_formula()\ntest_faster()\n<span class=\"hljs-built_in\">print</span>(<span class=\"hljs-string\">&quot;PASS&quot;</span>)</code></pre></div>\n<h2 id=\"exercises\">Exercises</h2>\n\n<div class=\"exercise\"><div class=\"ex-q\"><p>Your sensor reads 2 % high. With a loop gain of 20, what is the actual output error in closed loop?</p>\n</div><details><summary>Show the solution</summary><div class=\"ex-s\"><p>The loop drives the measurement to the reference, so the true output settles about 2 % low (more exactly, <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.1389em;\">T</span><span class=\"mord\">/</span><span class=\"mopen\">(</span><span class=\"mord\">1.02</span><span class=\"mclose\">)</span></span></span></span> of the target). Feedback can’t correct sensor errors: the output is only as good as the measurement.</p>\n</div></details></div>\n\n<div class=\"exercise\"><div class=\"ex-q\"><p>How large must the loop gain be for a 50 % plant gain change to cause under 1 % output change?</p>\n</div><details><summary>Show the solution</summary><div class=\"ex-s\"><p>For large changes use the exact form: output ratio <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:1.53em;vertical-align:-0.52em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mopen nulldelimiter\"></span><span class=\"mfrac\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:1.01em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.655em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\">L</span><span class=\"mord mtight\">/</span><span class=\"mopen mtight\">(</span><span class=\"mord mtight\">1</span><span class=\"mbin mtight\">+</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\">L</span><span class=\"mclose mtight\">)</span></span></span></span><span style=\"top:-3.23em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"frac-line\" style=\"border-bottom-width:0.04em;\"></span></span><span style=\"top:-3.485em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">1.5</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\">L</span><span class=\"mord mtight\">/</span><span class=\"mopen mtight\">(</span><span class=\"mord mtight\">1</span><span class=\"mbin mtight\">+</span><span class=\"mord mtight\">1.5</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\">L</span><span class=\"mclose mtight\">)</span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.52em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mclose nulldelimiter\"></span></span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:1.4133em;vertical-align:-0.4033em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mopen nulldelimiter\"></span><span class=\"mfrac\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:1.01em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.655em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">1</span><span class=\"mbin mtight\">+</span><span class=\"mord mtight\">1.5</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\">L</span></span></span></span><span style=\"top:-3.23em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"frac-line\" style=\"border-bottom-width:0.04em;\"></span></span><span style=\"top:-3.485em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">1.5</span><span class=\"mopen mtight\">(</span><span class=\"mord mtight\">1</span><span class=\"mbin mtight\">+</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\">L</span><span class=\"mclose mtight\">)</span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.4033em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mclose nulldelimiter\"></span></span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">&lt;</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6444em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">1.01</span></span></span></span>. Solving: <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.7278em;vertical-align:-0.0833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">1.5</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">+</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.7224em;vertical-align:-0.0391em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">1.5</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">L</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">&lt;</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.7278em;vertical-align:-0.0833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">1.01</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">+</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">1.515</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">L</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">⇒</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.7224em;vertical-align:-0.0391em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">L</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">&gt;</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6444em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">32.7</span></span></span></span>. With <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0576em;\">S</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">≈</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">1/</span><span class=\"mopen\">(</span><span class=\"mord\">1</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">+</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">L</span><span class=\"mclose\">)</span></span></span></span> and <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">Δ</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">G</span><span class=\"mord\">/</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">G</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6444em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">0.5</span></span></span></span> the first-order estimate gives <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.7224em;vertical-align:-0.0391em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">L</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">&gt;</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6444em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">49</span></span></span></span>, which is conservative for an increase.</p>\n</div></details></div>\n<h2 id=\"quiz\">Quiz</h2>\n\n<div class=\"quiz\" data-quiz=\"p13-l01\"></div>\n","toc":[{"id":"open-loop-needs-a-perfect-model","title":"Open loop needs a perfect model"},{"id":"closed-loop","title":"Closed loop"},{"id":"worked-example","title":"Worked example"},{"id":"code-it-from-scratch","title":"Code it from scratch"},{"id":"exercises","title":"Exercises"},{"id":"quiz","title":"Quiz"}],"quiz":[{"id":"p13-l01-q1","type":"num","q":"<p>Closed-loop DC gain with a loop gain of 20?</p>\n","explain":"<p>L/(1 + L).</p>\n","answer":0.9524,"tol":0.001,"unit":""},{"id":"p13-l01-q2","type":"num","q":"<p>Sensitivity S at DC with a loop gain of 20?</p>\n","explain":"<p>1/(1 + L).</p>\n","answer":0.0476,"tol":0.002,"unit":""},{"id":"p13-l01-q3","type":"num","q":"<p>Output error in % with the prefilter when the plant gain is 30 % high (L goes from 20 to 26)?</p>\n","explain":"<p>About 27 times less than open loop.</p>\n","answer":1.11,"tol":0.01,"unit":"%"},{"id":"p13-l01-q4","type":"num","q":"<p>Closed-loop time constant in ms for τ = 0.5 s and L = 20?</p>\n","explain":"<p>τ/(1 + L).</p>\n","answer":23.8,"tol":0.01,"unit":"ms"},{"id":"p13-l01-q5","type":"mc","q":"<p>What can feedback not correct?</p>\n","explain":"<p>The loop tracks the measured value.</p>\n","options":["errors in the sensor","changes in plant gain","slow plant dynamics","load disturbances"],"answer":0},{"id":"p13-l01-q6","type":"mc","q":"<p>What is the main risk of raising loop gain?</p>\n","explain":"<p>Dynamics and delays make high gain oscillate.</p>\n","options":["instability","lower accuracy","higher sensitivity to plant changes","slower response"],"answer":0}],"code":[{"file":"feedback.py","lang":"python","src":"import numpy as np\n\ntau, G0 = 0.5, 2.0\nK = 10.0\nL0 = K * G0\npre = (1 + L0) / L0                       # prefilter: nominal closed loop has unit DC gain\n\ndef simulate(Gtrue, closed, T=3.0, dt=1e-4, r=1.0):\n    y, out = 0.0, []\n    for _ in range(int(T / dt)):\n        u = K * (pre * r - y) if closed else r / G0\n        y += dt * (Gtrue * u - y) / tau    # first-order plant, exact enough at this step\n        out.append(y)\n    return np.array(out)\n\ndef test_closed_loop_error_ten_times_smaller():\n    for change in (+0.3, -0.3):\n        Gt = G0 * (1 + change)\n        e_open = abs(simulate(Gt, False)[-1] - 1)\n        e_closed = abs(simulate(Gt, True)[-1] - 1)\n        Lt = K * Gt\n        predicted = abs(Lt / (1 + Lt) * pre - 1)\n        print(f\"plant gain {change:+.0%}: open-loop error {e_open:.1%}, closed-loop {e_closed:.2%} (predicted {predicted:.2%}), {e_open / e_closed:.0f}x smaller\")\n        assert abs(e_closed - predicted) < 1e-4\n        assert e_open / e_closed > 10\n\ndef test_sensitivity_formula():\n    for L in (1.0, 5.0, 20.0, 100.0):\n        T = lambda g: g * L / (1 + g * L)\n        d = 1e-6\n        rel = (T(1 + d) - T(1 - d)) / (2 * d) / T(1)\n        assert abs(rel - 1 / (1 + L)) < 1e-8\n\ndef test_faster():\n    y = simulate(G0, True, T=0.5)\n    t63 = np.argmax(y > 0.632 * y[-1]) * 1e-4\n    print(f\"closed-loop time constant {t63 * 1000:.1f} ms (predicted {tau / (1 + L0) * 1000:.1f} ms)\")\n    assert abs(t63 - tau / (1 + L0)) < 5e-4\n\ntest_closed_loop_error_ten_times_smaller()\ntest_sensitivity_formula()\ntest_faster()\nprint(\"PASS\")"}]}